      "id": "claim_23e64628509b4791a75c7cc368d6cc0b",
      "statement": "parse_confidence is a blend of a saturating length component and the ratio of text-bearing blocks, then capped when characters-per-page fall below a floor (catching a parser silently losing some pages), capped again when the pdfplumber fallback was adopted, and finally multiplied by (1 - cid_fraction) so a half-unreadable document cannot report high confidence.",
